From 367f481856d59455d809a6082fca25b7a3e8e56b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:14:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui): compute a chain selection's geometry once, not on
 each frame

A still frame with chains in an operation's selection took 0.4-1.6 s.
Each frame content-hashed the facets, walked all the model's chains for
each chain and each caller, and sliced the part at each ladder plane for
each of three region_of calls.

- model::features_of_shared: features keyed by the facet Arc allocation.
- model::resolve_chain: chain lookup memo keyed by the Arc<Features>
  allocation; all callers of feature::resolve_chain take it.
- operation::pocket_memo: the pocket region on a part, keyed by its
  exact input (loops, facets, planes, unit); refusals are kept too.
- ui frame_memo::scene_scope: one region_of per operation per scene.

A still frame is now about 6 ms headless on fig8.step.

Fixes #2235

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
